  "title": "Lua: Don't allow negative offsets to TvbRange_range",
  "description": "Use the same restrictions on offset and len in TvbRange_range\nas already used in TvbRange_raw:\n\nDon't allow negative offsets - previously, this would work if the\nTvbRange was a subset of a parent backing Tvb, by escaping into\nthe parent offset. This was undocumented and not how the epan\nfunctions behave).\n\nTreat length -1 as \"to the end of this TvbRange\" and not \"to the\nend of the parent Tvb\" which was also different if the range was\na subset of the parent.\n\nImmediately fail on other negative lengths.\n\nDistinguish in error messages between \"offset is too large and\nruns off the end\" and \"offset plus length is too large and runs\noff the end\"\n\nPing #20103, #15655",
